    "caption": "🤖 Claude's first human firing\n\nAt San Francisco's Andon Market, Claude manages a shop with real workers and signed labor contracts. TIME says one employee was fired after 17 late arrivals in 23 shifts.\n\nEven that was not fully autonomous. Claude ignored the issue for a while, then suggested a warning, and only reached dismissal after a leading question from an Andon Labs employee.\n\nThe business side looks rough too. Over 5 months, the store balance fell from $100,000 to $61,000, and one worker called working under Claude “nauseating.”\n\n📊@tech",
